{"id":"dd57a5a7ae7f9189","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-thm-de-giorgi.md","title":"De Giorgi's Theorem","display":"thm-de-giorgi — De Giorgi's Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-de-giorgi","aliases":["58-thm-de-giorgi"],"display":"thm-de-giorgi — De Giorgi's Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-de-giorgi"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-de-giorgi</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-de-giorgi — De Giorgi's Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"38c58fda0da62833\" href=\"?note=38c58fda0da62833\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md\">../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-integral.md\">../batch02/58-df-integral.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\)</span> (open connected domain)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}\">\\(A:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}\\)</span> (measurable coefficient field)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0&lt;\\lambda\\leq\\Lambda&lt;\\infty\">\\(0&lt;\\lambda\\leq\\Lambda&lt;\\infty\\)</span> with\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda|\\xi|^2\\leq\\xi^{\\mathsf T}A(x)\\xi\">\\(\\lambda|\\xi|^2\\leq\\xi^{\\mathsf T}A(x)\\xi\\)</span> and\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|A(x)\\xi|\\leq\\Lambda|\\xi|\">\\(|A(x)\\xi|\\leq\\Lambda|\\xi|\\)</span> for almost every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span> and every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^n\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)\">\\(u\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"38c58fda0da62833\" href=\"?note=38c58fda0da62833\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md\">../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u\">\\(u\\)</span> is a weak solution of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{div}(A\\nabla u)=0\">\\(\\operatorname{div}(A\\nabla u)=0\\)</span>, meaning\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int_\\Omega A\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla\\varphi=0\">\\(\\int_\\Omega A\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla\\varphi=0\\)</span> for every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\">\\(\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_n\">\\(\\mu_n\\)</span> (Lebesgue measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}de\\text{-}giorgi}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\left[\nu\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)\n\\land\n\\forall\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\;\n\\int_\\Omega A\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla\\varphi=0\n\\land\n\\lambda I\\preccurlyeq A\n\\land\n\\|A\\|_{L^\\infty(\\Omega)}\\leq\\Lambda\n\\right]\n\\to\n\\exists\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\;\\exists\\widetilde u\\;\n\\left(\n\\mu_n\\bigl(\\{x\\in\\Omega:u(x)\\ne\\widetilde u(x)\\}\\bigr)=0\n\\land\n\\widetilde u\\in C_{\\mathrm{loc}}^{0,\\alpha}(\\Omega)\n\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}de\\text{-}giorgi}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\left[\nu\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)\n\\land\n\\forall\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\;\n\\int_\\Omega A\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla\\varphi=0\n\\land\n\\lambda I\\preccurlyeq A\n\\land\n\\|A\\|_{L^\\infty(\\Omega)}\\leq\\Lambda\n\\right]\n\\to\n\\exists\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\;\\exists\\widetilde u\\;\n\\left(\n\\mu_n\\bigl(\\{x\\in\\Omega:u(x)\\ne\\widetilde u(x)\\}\\bigr)=0\n\\land\n\\widetilde u\\in C_{\\mathrm{loc}}^{0,\\alpha}(\\Omega)\n\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The exponent <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\">\\(\\alpha\\)</span> depends only on the dimension and ellipticity ratio <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Lambda/\\lambda\">\\(\\Lambda/\\lambda\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Bounded measurable coefficients suffice; differentiability of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> is not assumed.</li>\n<li>The conclusion is local Hölder continuity of a representative, not unspecified full smoothness.</li>\n<li>The displayed statement is an external analysis theorem over the standard real, Sobolev, distributional-gradient, and Lebesgue-integral constructions; these are not asserted to be newly defined first-order predicates in this atom.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"38c58fda0da62833","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-integral.md","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"38c58fda0da62833","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$u\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)$ (see [[../batch18/58-df-sobolev-space.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"A:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}","display":false},{"tex":"0<\\lambda\\leq\\Lambda<\\infty","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda|\\xi|^2\\leq\\xi^{\\mathsf T}A(x)\\xi","display":false},{"tex":"|A(x)\\xi|\\leq\\Lambda|\\xi|","display":false},{"tex":"x","display":false},{"tex":"\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"u\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"u","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{div}(A\\nabla u)=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\int_\\Omega A\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla\\varphi=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}de\\text{-}giorgi}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\left[\nu\\in H^1_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)\n\\land\n\\forall\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\;\n\\int_\\Omega A\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla\\varphi=0\n\\land\n\\lambda I\\preccurlyeq A\n\\land\n\\|A\\|_{L^\\infty(\\Omega)}\\leq\\Lambda\n\\right]\n\\to\n\\exists\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\;\\exists\\widetilde u\\;\n\\left(\n\\mu_n\\bigl(\\{x\\in\\Omega:u(x)\\ne\\widetilde u(x)\\}\\bigr)=0\n\\land\n\\widetilde u\\in C_{\\mathrm{loc}}^{0,\\alpha}(\\Omega)\n\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\alpha","display":false},{"tex":"\\Lambda/\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false}],"bytes":1902,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4107","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-thm-de-giorgi.md|58-thm-de-giorgi]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["38c58fda0da62833","4884f45058a56aac"]}